    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0138" n="872" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg872"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thurston to Mr. Gresham.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hawaiian Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington, D.
                                C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-02-26"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 26,
                    1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With farther reference to the alleged
                    violation of the United States neutrality laws by Captain Martin of the schooner
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Wahlberg</hi>, I have the honor to inform you that I
                    have received from Mr. Wilder, Hawaiian consul at San Francisco, a further
                    statement concerning the witnesses. He states that he has found a deck hand of
                    the tug alleged to have delivered the arms on board of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wahlberg</hi>, who makes a clear and direct statement,
                    making a valuable witness. He further states that the cook and mate of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wahlberg</hi> were discharged from the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wahlberg</hi> upon her recent arrival at San Diego, and
                    are now in San Francisco; also, that all of these men are liable to ship on
                    outgoing vessels at an early date, so that if their evidence is to be obtained
                    it will have to be soon, or it will become unavailable.</p>
                <p>With renewed assurances, etc.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">L. A. Thurston.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
